# Checkboxes

Use checkboxes for independent selections or a single on/off preference.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## Choose selection before control

The [forms decision guide](controls.html#choose-the-control-by-its-meaning) distinguishes independent selections, mutually exclusive answers and physical commands. This page owns independent checkbox selection. A checked item in a form is an answer; any immediate-save preference must clearly state its persistence behaviour and must not silently issue a device command.

## When to use it

Use a group when several rooms can be included in a view. A single checkbox can express a reversible preference such as muted colours. Explain whether several choices are allowed.

## When not to use it

Do not use a checkbox group for a single choice such as temperature units. Avoid a bulk-selection control when there are only two clear options.

## Home Assistant adaptation

When editing an existing Home Assistant preference, show its saved checked state. This differs from preselecting answers to a new question, which can conceal a missed decision. Keep presentation preferences separate from physical commands. Checking a room in a filter must not switch its devices on.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a fieldset and legend for related options, visible associated labels, and a predictable focus order. Make the whole label a generous target. If an exclusive “no rooms” option is introduced, enforce that rule on submission as well as in JavaScript.

